[{:db/id "q-125237/selection/1299814cbaac5ae09b24256f92e5a2654028d131ba799a388b0e2e50d0a90db0" :answer/id #uuid "a062fd1a-a751-5522-9439-7c2d18fd2251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125237/selection/0350ccd89237b8a0350a6e87609466cc2e0ec2708d39c072f1f7986285949283" :answer/id #uuid "df0c4859-5dea-5999-8d14-38364fcd450d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125237/selection/3f6ccee9113760f7bdb06ee224208ee588c8e1d67adc6c48073902f4885fc134" :answer/id #uuid "75e29608-d101-5e74-a0f9-aeb93dacd868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125237/selection/3086b3b25a4822a3fcf8b89a0f1d0fdf2ea34692590f9564716cbbab3515bf22" :answer/id #uuid "24c7d6cd-76f1-5136-b989-3e280d92b241" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125237/selection/d8d607c1d386b6513804ec437f87a1e8a060e073e9d677b6112fc16fdc948fb6" :answer/id #uuid "19ceeb92-e248-5e16-81d4-f63546d4c29a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(c)=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125237/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "121e061c-8f59-5d38-a696-c7283ddd23ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125237/selection/3086b3b25a4822a3fcf8b89a0f1d0fdf2ea34692590f9564716cbbab3515bf22" :answer-field/choices ["q-125237/selection/1299814cbaac5ae09b24256f92e5a2654028d131ba799a388b0e2e50d0a90db0" "q-125237/selection/0350ccd89237b8a0350a6e87609466cc2e0ec2708d39c072f1f7986285949283" "q-125237/selection/3f6ccee9113760f7bdb06ee224208ee588c8e1d67adc6c48073902f4885fc134" "q-125237/selection/3086b3b25a4822a3fcf8b89a0f1d0fdf2ea34692590f9564716cbbab3515bf22" "q-125237/selection/d8d607c1d386b6513804ec437f87a1e8a060e073e9d677b6112fc16fdc948fb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125237" :question/id #uuid "70a9e682-5225-5573-9ac6-75c97731ce3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-125237" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/74850221ee168c6911ee5b6c319d2128f67149f81790528940822e253905fc0f.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,3).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following:\n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-5$ and $b=3.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-5)}{3-(-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2}{3+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n *The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{1}{2}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125237/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8756e5e-3ce4-5c02-8700-8e2f3fa81e9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125237"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349/selection/0e208701b5a0b5ecc0da6c7ec2ac0ab9e1b355dae94c6080ea447dbe02408a75" :answer/id #uuid "fc868210-90c8-5aef-8a96-299b3c7236db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349/selection/d8d607c1d386b6513804ec437f87a1e8a060e073e9d677b6112fc16fdc948fb6" :answer/id #uuid "ac7a81f8-6c26-5bac-a646-1a6beefe08f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(c)=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349/selection/97295b2495f8b2dd8986be13d2b0cc398f05bfee964a8f04c350659f91433a3c" :answer/id #uuid "d3e66a85-4cec-555e-926c-267fb5074e37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349/selection/df1605eef366e8bf06cf872d3fed3c4bbb7958354106e5d10a8141a12c8f5cf8" :answer/id #uuid "9c20212e-f576-5a79-9ba2-8ed2dbe1b52c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{9}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349/selection/5f82971e0ef42641aa2bbbbaf028243d6155d0d967b2eceda8eaf40e4b1249e3" :answer/id #uuid "dd764a30-26f8-5243-9774-99f981dcac04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52164d79-ea96-5cd6-a8b0-6bd7485d4f2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73349/selection/5f82971e0ef42641aa2bbbbaf028243d6155d0d967b2eceda8eaf40e4b1249e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-73349/selection/0e208701b5a0b5ecc0da6c7ec2ac0ab9e1b355dae94c6080ea447dbe02408a75" "q-73349/selection/d8d607c1d386b6513804ec437f87a1e8a060e073e9d677b6112fc16fdc948fb6" "q-73349/selection/97295b2495f8b2dd8986be13d2b0cc398f05bfee964a8f04c350659f91433a3c" "q-73349/selection/df1605eef366e8bf06cf872d3fed3c4bbb7958354106e5d10a8141a12c8f5cf8" "q-73349/selection/5f82971e0ef42641aa2bbbbaf028243d6155d0d967b2eceda8eaf40e4b1249e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73349" :question/id #uuid "37d9c80f-2cd5-546e-9463-84b02d5e64b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-73349" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/6393810d90b8d340dbde041c43cb7e146cb59fedfcfd4a678827d291ea502b00.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,4]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,4).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following: \n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-5$ and $b=4.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(4)-f(-5)}{4-(-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-2}{4+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n *The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,4)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{5}{9}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73349/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8756e5e-3ce4-5c02-8700-8e2f3fa81e9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73349"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73347/selection/64d675c1fb8eda8c5c5ad1bc4a20858d4834d27d06242ad3fb51fece1cd180eb" :answer/id #uuid "17c32529-9e53-5d90-8272-8935f96c8073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73347/selection/a6b52154d0a3c5b4ae442c1a6dbe499ea4554ebc9e06a490fd04e69607f763ec" :answer/id #uuid "184e1cad-db35-586e-8096-d194bc747a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73347/selection/3f6ccee9113760f7bdb06ee224208ee588c8e1d67adc6c48073902f4885fc134" :answer/id #uuid "5b3dd974-3859-5997-b842-ba0d9266bf26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73347/selection/8c452e73ec2572d15a17ad0c8dee9cec63bf71908b7042c934a8014c8ab3f23b" :answer/id #uuid "cb6f4868-7567-578e-aac7-d488b84dd788" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73347/selection/3086b3b25a4822a3fcf8b89a0f1d0fdf2ea34692590f9564716cbbab3515bf22" :answer/id #uuid "018d6c31-fb5c-5