{2}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8756e5e-3ce4-5c02-8700-8e2f3fa81e9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248/selection/3086b3b25a4822a3fcf8b89a0f1d0fdf2ea34692590f9564716cbbab3515bf22" :answer/id #uuid "6905de7c-f7b0-5979-b8e4-58e9d68cf32d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248/selection/1299814cbaac5ae09b24256f92e5a2654028d131ba799a388b0e2e50d0a90db0" :answer/id #uuid "b81dd9d1-2226-597a-b188-0db108e1c1dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248/selection/01c8aa0b6aa9fc9898f151e83249ad96dc36ea17775dbb6648ba8999004f212d" :answer/id #uuid "962c4765-f0a7-57f9-8976-ab62d2db87db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248/selection/8568fb007800f3a2fa79c4ebe80bece362f90db388b590fbb7e90c02e65e69b5" :answer/id #uuid "e3573e14-19e0-5c9c-a6e6-36841c51566b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248/selection/5ce6a45ff589084e70e90cdc5c7f85cb33cbf4f3106487af18aeb08b353e2c0e" :answer/id #uuid "3a98326d-fe3b-5aba-a3d6-d56d84d691bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d168ce8e-68b1-57fa-a4c9-359abe9c5940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125248/selection/8568fb007800f3a2fa79c4ebe80bece362f90db388b590fbb7e90c02e65e69b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-125248/selection/3086b3b25a4822a3fcf8b89a0f1d0fdf2ea34692590f9564716cbbab3515bf22" "q-125248/selection/1299814cbaac5ae09b24256f92e5a2654028d131ba799a388b0e2e50d0a90db0" "q-125248/selection/01c8aa0b6aa9fc9898f151e83249ad96dc36ea17775dbb6648ba8999004f212d" "q-125248/selection/8568fb007800f3a2fa79c4ebe80bece362f90db388b590fbb7e90c02e65e69b5" "q-125248/selection/5ce6a45ff589084e70e90cdc5c7f85cb33cbf4f3106487af18aeb08b353e2c0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125248" :question/id #uuid "2d260f0c-bd30-5d1a-82e3-cbb85eb5bedb" :question/math-academy-id "q-125248" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/ec58e17c04427988e634bebdece555ad782be504bd0734dbd7ffd5b1b95bc760.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,3).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following: \n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-5$ and $b=3.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-5)}{3-(-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-3)}{3+5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n *The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{1}{8}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125248/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8756e5e-3ce4-5c02-8700-8e2f3fa81e9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125248"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354/selection/7cb5259ed3a0683818659485c90bbc2104c92544d483e5a839b7b62bd1e4d759" :answer/id #uuid "9b2d3ddb-93d5-5d4d-9b86-b078b3600fa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(c)=-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354/selection/00b83ccea8ba738a0338aadaafd5714f9c210bcb942168d3d3fe5f92db349fba" :answer/id #uuid "807eff2f-33f9-5678-87ed-4ec523447a95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{8}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354/selection/2d3c03973f8e17de7c3e89034a88fd4acc5595fe66baadf00ff3e8b0e733c4ee" :answer/id #uuid "6f8443f2-f2bb-5db0-93f6-66a50a9920df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354/selection/742c246eef7b65dda219706ce84adadaaa0b9c334374601c95f33ad09d314608" :answer/id #uuid "7aad2e0d-d3c8-552f-a49e-c35b2a0b0b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354/selection/14e3f3e433076d44b72281655ac7525e0baef1f546b8cba19333b1dc06488479" :answer/id #uuid "16c1ff25-221b-595c-b770-a6c70a3c76a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0422f357-1fa3-5fa9-9b29-4197de680874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73354/selection/742c246eef7b65dda219706ce84adadaaa0b9c334374601c95f33ad09d314608" :answer-field/choices ["q-73354/selection/7cb5259ed3a0683818659485c90bbc2104c92544d483e5a839b7b62bd1e4d759" "q-73354/selection/00b83ccea8ba738a0338aadaafd5714f9c210bcb942168d3d3fe5f92db349fba" "q-73354/selection/2d3c03973f8e17de7c3e89034a88fd4acc5595fe66baadf00ff3e8b0e733c4ee" "q-73354/selection/742c246eef7b65dda219706ce84adadaaa0b9c334374601c95f33ad09d314608" "q-73354/selection/14e3f3e433076d44b72281655ac7525e0baef1f546b8cba19333b1dc06488479"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73354" :question/id #uuid "75e8bebf-29a4-5c2b-8823-7c997148cfbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73354" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/029a51dccba9f1ec927c820fb8adb72e926b88a881f4646090ac651ef29da271.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on $(-5,3).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following:\n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-5$ and $b=3.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-5)}{3-(-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{3+5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{8}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73354/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8756e5e-3ce4-5c02-8700-8e2f3fa81e9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73354"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-2344"] :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for \n $f(x)=-3\\sqrt{x}+2$ on the interval $[0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,2]$ and differentiable on $(0,2),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (0,2)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=0$ and $b=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(2)-f(0)}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3\\sqrt{2}+2)-(-3\\sqrt{0}+2)}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\sqrt{x}+2)=-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{c}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{c}} & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{c}} & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ c & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "67427346-3ea0-5b13-b931-b7414820c29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0a94857f-1624-5820-94b9-6f525a7eaac8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "a6245ad7-2d47-5544-aada-ffffa59b4325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "ca4689be-f51c-534e-9612-8361bb585b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "77e98f3b-efce-556b-9825-d61cd1f29838" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8be1f33a-6b9a-5b58-972e-22a94646a1fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2305/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-2305/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-2305/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-2305/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-2305/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-2305/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2305" :question/id #uuid "5f9d35ca-8f34-57a2-b6aa-de34e247b461" :question/math-academy-id "q-2305" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for  $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+x-2$ on the interval $[-1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,2]$ and differentiable on $(-1,2),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (-1,2)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=-1$ and $b=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(2)-f(-1)}{2-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot {2}^{2}+2-2)-(3\\cdot (-1)^{2}+(-1)-2)}{2+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-0}{3} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}+x-2)=6x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=6c+1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6c+1 & =4 \\\\ 6c & =3 \\\\ c & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2305/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2305"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-2341"] :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for \n $f(x)={x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-8,6].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-8,6]$ and differentiable on $(-8,6).$ \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (-8,6)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=-8$ and $b=6$ into the above gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(6)-f(-8)}{6-(-8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-(-8)^{2}}{14} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2c & =-2 \\\\ c & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342/selection/1d181f16f4185f1243f6368f60e3d9d979921ba3e431470c8054f0fb4975fe88" :answer/id #uuid "fbb75918-34d8-5024-82b4-b9392f2119fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\,,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342/selection/2e8122050bd469de4838283dc62870eaee064092147a995061b03ca4f1155909" :answer/id #uuid "8c88a1ac-4c20-508f-aab6-31c06f787e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}\\," :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "dc332d90-894b-531a-9c8f-2fb91cf04a05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342/selection/f4f061696e26034fa6b5e0ad920585c9b4e3bf29a4ed2186f51a4eb4c531a745" :answer/id #uuid "1cda0e1a-40fc-5872-bd05-97da86b8a904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\," :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342/selection/ecceb8c7c319c997791529253916bc7c9ed93947c80091bc40561a42061df09e" :answer/id #uuid "591d829f-6048-5881-bff8-c4aef2776230" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e68ded2-3d31-5158-9654-23c0cf579fae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2342/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-2342/selection/1d181f16f4185f1243f6368f60e3d9d979921ba3e431470c8054f0fb4975fe88" "q-2342/selection/2e8122050bd469de4838283dc62870eaee064092147a995061b03ca4f1155909" "q-2342/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-2342/selection/f4f061696e26034fa6b5e0ad920585c9b4e3bf29a4ed2186f51a4eb4c531a745" "q-2342/selection/ecceb8c7c319c997791529253916bc7c9ed93947c80091bc40561a42061df09e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2342" :question/id #uuid "3da87fee-0786-5e85-9e1d-628e337cb883" :question/math-academy-id "q-2342" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for \n $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+5$ on the interval $[1,4].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[1,4]$ and differentiable on $(1,4),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (1,4)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=1$ and $b=4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(4)-f(1)}{4-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{({4}^{2}-2\\cdot 4+5)-({1}^{2}-2\\cdot 1+5)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13-4}{3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-2x+5)=2x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=2c-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2c-2 & =3 \\\\ 2c & =5 \\\\ c & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2342/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2342"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345063/field-1/2ee71f97da76a36a5f98bee4ae2425715bbc4597486731aaed28becb23704cce" :answer/id #uuid "c5416af2-c5a6-5183-8a75-14862a9fb852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345063/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a11827e-ce9d-5354-a735-fdc0d1a904b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345063/field-1/2ee71f97da76a36a5f98bee4ae2425715bbc4597486731aaed28becb23704cce" :answer-field/choices ["q-345063/field-1/2ee71f97da76a36a5f98bee4ae2425715bbc4597486731aaed28becb23704cce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345063" :question/id #uuid "ba9aff4f-f2e6-5d6a-bbda-2b487e4d8919" :question/math-academy-id "q-345063" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for $f(x)=5\\sqrt{x}-2$ on the interval $[4,9].$\n\n$c=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[4,9]$ and differentiable on $(4,9),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (4,9)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=4$ and $b=9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(9)-f(4)}{9-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5\\sqrt{9}-2)-(5\\sqrt{4}-2)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{13-8}{5} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\sqrt{x}-2)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{c}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{c}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ c & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} \\\\ c & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345063/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345063"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77888/selection/f4288a1e1e7b3cd434deaaa7015cb6d327e588af8ba3d59126ebe640a8019788" :