satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Hence, $h(x)$ is not continuous on $[-1,1].$ Therefore, $h(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $p(x)$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\pm 1.$ Hence, $p(x)$ is not continuous on $[-1,1].$ Therefore, $p(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $s(x)$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\pm 1.$ Hence, $s(x)$ is not continuous on $[-1,1].$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125317/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "999d8587-8f15-5871-81dd-26c0c0ae063e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48399/selection/7b9ec6a7237846228b88e9e1a3d22fe9e0abb2b8611aacc89e22a2b7b511402d" :answer/id #uuid "86071fc5-6aa6-5231-86fa-5b74f5be5e27" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/66663e046f3c00d3f4884b7129cdc5b5d4be18574c6f2fc47fd39dcc976e398c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48399/selection/05bba98e33ee870f3cd1d0dc64cba20ce153bfb567c4f482c1d920c7ee88b46a" :answer/id #uuid "3e0e4c7c-830f-5964-85e7-b5bb9f9c8b90" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/e6ccc7f465d50c13059b93e1b12b80bc3c10b9970ea0fedd5a3b3b9d4d3cabf5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48399/selection/75f6cbe5b518b925d66b0c59968fa3fe6369f79a6068fbe39e83c1f3219676cb" :answer/id #uuid "7e33c55a-951d-5be8-9254-ffffa294fe6b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/fab6a73c970500b896e38e75faf21c1fd5aecf9909